  "description": "TEPTAL crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: H24 Cr2 Dy4 O40 S6 2-,C4 H12 N2 2+,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2B (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1B (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.910-4.488 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.06-145.05°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula (pipzH2)[Cr2Dy4(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)4(H2O)10(μ3-SO4)4(SO4)2]·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 10 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
